# TypeScript / JavaScript

- Use the repo's existing test runner and `npm`/`pnpm`/`yarn` scripts; do not add new test frameworks.
- Prefer `async`/`await`; handle promise rejections at boundaries the repo already uses.
- Avoid `any` unless the codebase already uses it for that layer; match strictness of nearby files.
- Do not change `tsconfig`, bundler, or ESLint config unless the task requires it.
- For DOM/browser APIs, verify types against current lib definitions rather than guessing.
- Keep imports aligned with existing path aliases (`@/`, `~/`, etc.).
- When adding exports, match named vs default export style of sibling files.
